<title>RUSSIA: Russian 133-day T-bill yields 30.39 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 133-day T-bill yields 30.39 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an additional 133-day tranche of GKO discount Treasury bills was 30.39 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had predicted the yield between 28.47 and 29.90 percent.</p>
<p>The original issue closed at 90.46 on Tuesday to yield 28.73 percent. Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number	    22069 (additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume	     4.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	    1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	   4.31 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	   3.20 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		   2.88 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	    90.03 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price  89.86 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	    30.39 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield 30.97 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	133 days</p>
<p>    Original issue date    February 5, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date	    July 16, 1997</p>
<p>The original issue was the first to be subject to a new 15-percent tax on earnings on government securities.</p>
<p>On March 5, the Finance Ministry also raised 5.75 trillion roubles ($1 billion) by selling 238-day T-bills, making total proceeds from today's auctions 8.63 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>It had repaid 8.60 trillion roubles of maturing 210-day T-bills (series 22044).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($ = 5696 Russian Roubles)</p>
